  <cac:TenderingProcess>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">The procurement includes one institution place with 24 hour care and treatment for one user. The service shall be provided based on a lifetime need and it includes: 24 hour staffed institution place with a minimum of 1:1 staffing. Individually facilitated follow-up of mental and somatic health, including handling medicines and dietary supervision. Practical assistance and guidance for daily tasks, personal hygiene, financial management and social participation. Facilitating activities and social contact, as well as support for developing and maintaining a network. Interaction with relevant health and care services, as well as support in contact with public bodies. The agreement shall be entered into based on a lifetime need for institution sites. The contract can be terminated if the need for institution space is no longer present, or if the user wishes to end their stay. The contract shall be evaluated annually and it will be adjusted or terminated in accordance with changed requirements, in dialogue with users and relevant professional bodies.</cbc:Description>
  </cac:TenderingProcess>
  <cac:ProcurementProject>
    <cbc:ID>VÅ-25-07</cbc:ID>
    
    <cbc:Name languageID="ENG">VÅ-25-07 2017 Institution Place</cbc:Name>
    
    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">The aim of the procurement is to ensure a uniform, stable and professionally responsible 24 hour institution place for a user with a compound mental and somatic disease picture, where the need for care and treatment is assessed as lifelong. The institution square shall contribute to safeguarding the user's health, quality of life and dignity, and at the same time ensure the necessary follow-up, supervision and facilitation in accordance with the current legislation and professional guidelines.</cbc:Description>
